{"ts": "2026-11-11T03:31:13.383Z", "task": "T-2026-11-11-0132-setup-options-bc", "event": "risk_recorded", "actor": "agent", "runtime": "claude", "stage": "implementation", "detail": "R-local-memory-md-says-only-rr-setup-opens-d6ca: local-memory.md says only /rr-setup opens the memory decision", "data": {"rkey": "R-local-memory-md-says-only-rr-setup-opens-d6ca", "title": "local-memory.md says only /rr-setup opens the memory decision", "where": ["docs/local-memory.md:46"], "label": "RISK", "what": "The model may call 'decision open --kind setup' from any session or task (rr_state/dialog_cmd.py:66-68); only the human's pick of the shown memory enable command grants anything. Review L1, STRONG, T-2026-11-11-0132-setup-options-bc.", "likelihood": "low", "fix": "Say the model may open the setup decision and that only the human's pick of the shown command enables memory.", "status": "open", "status_why": null, "supersedes": null}}
{"ts": "2026-11-11T03:31:13.429Z", "task": "T-2026-11-11-0132-setup-options-bc", "event": "risk_recorded", "actor": "agent", "runtime": "claude", "stage": "implementation", "detail": "R-a-mismatched-memory-enable-does-not-void-7bef: a mismatched memory enable does not void the dialog picks", "data": {"rkey": "R-a-mismatched-memory-enable-does-not-void-7bef", "title": "a mismatched memory enable does not void the dialog picks", "where": ["hooks/guard/dialog.py:559-563"], "label": "RISK", "what": "guarded() and HUMAN_VERB_RE do not list memory enable, so while a decision is pending a variant gets DECISION_PENDING, not CONSENT_MISMATCH. Kept on purpose (spec: the gate is reused unchanged); state.py dialog_pick binds argv, ENTRY, root, session, window, an open decision and single use. Review L2.", "likelihood": "low", "fix": "Add memory enable to HUMAN_VERB_RE with a contract fixture, or state in R36.8 that it does not void.", "status": "open", "status_why": null, "supersedes": null}}
{"ts": "2026-11-11T03:31:13.470Z", "task": "T-2026-11-11-0132-setup-options-bc", "event": "risk_recorded", "actor": "agent", "runtime": "claude", "stage": "implementation", "detail": "R-rr-setup-fallback-hands-period-quarter-e-a1b3: rr-setup fallback hands --period quarter even when memory.json exists", "data": {"rkey": "R-rr-setup-fallback-hands-period-quarter-e-a1b3", "title": "rr-setup fallback hands --period quarter even when memory.json exists", "where": ["skills/rr-setup/SKILL.md:54-55"], "label": "RISK", "what": "The other-refusal fallback gives the human memory enable --period quarter unconditionally; under --options on a packages project it would rewrite the committed period for every teammate. setup.py's own fallback drops --period (setup.py:597-617). Review L3.", "likelihood": "low", "fix": "Say --period quarter only while memory.json is absent (R16).", "status": "open", "status_why": null, "supersedes": null}}
{"ts": "2026-11-11T03:31:13.513Z", "task": "T-2026-11-11-0132-setup-options-bc", "event": "risk_recorded", "actor": "agent", "runtime": "claude", "stage": "implementation", "detail": "R-memory-enable-through-a-pick-leaves-no-c-d0ba: memory enable through a pick leaves no committed record of who authorised it", "data": {"rkey": "R-memory-enable-through-a-pick-leaves-no-c-d0ba", "title": "memory enable through a pick leaves no committed record of who authorised it", "where": ["skills/ai-task/rr_state/memory_cmd.py:101-104"], "label": "RISK", "what": "Only stdout and the git-ignored consent.jsonl (a use by 'state.py memory', dialog.py:449) record it; a journal line exists only with a task in flight and a later DIALOG_SYNC command, while approve journals pick_data. Review L4.", "likelihood": "medium", "fix": "Journal a memory-enabled event with pick_data when a task is in flight, or mirror it into the packages record.", "status": "open", "status_why": null, "supersedes": null}}
{"ts": "2026-11-11T03:31:25.662Z", "task": "T-2026-11-11-0132-setup-options-bc", "event": "risk_recorded", "actor": "agent", "runtime": "claude", "stage": "implementation", "detail": "R-a-project-path-with-a-forbidden-label-ch-6745: a project path with a forbidden label character loses the whole setup dialog", "data": {"rkey": "R-a-project-path-with-a-forbidden-label-ch-6745", "title": "a project path with a forbidden label character loses the whole setup dialog", "where": ["skills/ai-task/rr_state/dialog_cmd.py:173-186"], "label": "RISK", "what": "The memory label carries the absolute project path; a LABEL_FORBIDDEN character (ampersand, semicolon, pipe, angle brackets, dollar-paren) or a label over 400 characters makes setup_open refuse the whole spec with exit 6, so runtime, survey and verify fall back to prose too. Fails closed. Review L5.", "likelihood": "low", "fix": "In setup.py, leave memory out of the dialog (fallback line only) when its label would fail validate_label.", "status": "open", "status_why": null, "supersedes": null}}
{"ts": "2026-11-11T03:31:25.702Z", "task": "T-2026-11-11-0132-setup-options-bc", "event": "risk_recorded", "actor": "agent", "runtime": "claude", "stage": "implementation", "detail": "R-dialog-pick-does-not-require-the-picked-d674: dialog_pick does not require the picked option to be a command", "data": {"rkey": "R-dialog-pick-does-not-require-the-picked-d674", "title": "dialog_pick does not require the picked option to be a command", "where": ["skills/ai-task/rr_state/dialog.py:444-447"], "label": "RISK", "what": "Any live pick whose label parses as this state.py's argv counts; check_setup_labels (dialog_cmd.py:206-208) is the only barrier between a choice that runs nothing and a grant. Pinned by test_setup_spec_rejects_foreign_command. Review I1.", "likelihood": "low", "fix": "In dialog_pick, also require the decision's option n to be of kind command.", "status": "open", "status_why": null, "supersedes": null}}
{"ts": "2026-11-11T03:31:25.750Z", "task": "T-2026-11-11-0132-setup-options-bc", "event": "risk_recorded", "actor": "agent", "runtime": "claude", "stage": "implementation", "detail": "R-a-verify-value-with-a-quote-dollar-or-ba-a6d9: a verify value with a quote, dollar or backslash breaks the skill's verify --set quoting", "data": {"rkey": "R-a-verify-value-with-a-quote-dollar-or-ba-a6d9", "title": "a verify value with a quote, dollar or backslash breaks the skill's verify --set quoting", "where": ["skills/rr-setup/SKILL.md:63"], "label": "RISK", "what": "The setup opener accepts any printable verify value shown in backticks in its own label (dialog_cmd.py:131-135); the skill passes it to setup.py verify --set in double quotes. setup.py's own candidates never contain those characters; only a hand-built spec reaches it. Review I2.", "likelihood": "low", "fix": "Refuse quote, dollar and backslash in verify values in the opener, or pass the value on stdin.", "status": "open", "status_why": null, "supersedes": null}}
